course: dictionary
lesson: 2050
title: Conqueror
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A conqueror is a person, army or country that takes control of a land or its people by force, or wins a war. Read the clues around the word. «In 1086 William the Conqueror had England's land, people and animals counted.» Counting the land and people after taking them tells you he took control of England.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. Someone who overcomes a difficulty is a conqueror, as in «the conqueror of Everest», the climber who reached the top. Ask yourself: did someone win a war, or did they beat something very hard? That tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Stories show conquerors in different ways. Some tell of heroes, and some tell of cruel invaders. It depends on who is telling the story. When you read about a conqueror, ask yourself whose side the writer is on.
fact: A conqueror is a noun. One is a conqueror, and more than one are conquerors.
fact: William the Conqueror invaded England and won at the Battle of Hastings.
fact: Alexander the Great and the Romans were famous conquerors.
fact: The Bible says Christians are «more than conquerors» through God's love.
fact: A conqueror can also be someone who overcomes a difficulty, like «the conqueror of Everest».
exercise: «In 1086 William the Conqueror had England's land, people and animals counted.» What is a conqueror here? | A small animal kept as a pet | *A person who takes control of a land or its people by force | A teacher who counts the class | A book that lists the land
exercise: Who is «the conqueror of Everest»? | *Someone who overcomes a difficulty by reaching the top | Someone who lives on a mountain | Someone who is afraid of heights | A climbing rope
exercise: What is the plural of conqueror, meaning more than one? | conquered | conquering | conqueror's | *conquerors
test: Stories show conquerors as heroes or as cruel invaders. Why might two stories about the same conqueror be different? | Because all stories are exactly the same | Because conquerors never really existed | *Because the people telling the story may see it differently | Because a conqueror is always a hero
test: The Bible says Christians are «more than conquerors». What is the best meaning? | They always win battles | They have taken control of land | *They overcome hard things through God's love | They are cruel invaders
exam: Which example best fits the first meaning of conqueror? | A cook who makes great cakes | A mouse who reads a history lesson | *Alexander the Great, who took control of many lands by force | A child who finished a jigsaw puzzle
